\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Figma \uc0\u8594  React in VS Code (3 Figma API calls)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Reusable starter for any Figma file. Copy the three scripts into a Vite + React app, fill in .env, and stop after:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 node scripts/generate-react.js --all
\f1\fs24 \
After that, all layout work is local. Do not call Figma again unless the design file actually changed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Why only 3 API calls?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Figma rate-limits tokens. The whole design is downloaded once, then everything else reads files on disk.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 1.
\f1\b0  node scripts/fetch-figma.js\uc0\u8232 API: GET /v1/files/:id/nodes?ids=\'85\u8232 Result: figma-node.json (layout, text, colors, sizes)\

\f0\b 2.
\f1\b0  node scripts/download-figma-images.js\uc0\u8232 API: GET /v1/files/:id/images\u8232 Result: URL map for photo / IMAGE fills\

\f0\b 3.
\f1\b0  same script\uc0\u8232 API: GET /v1/images/:id?format=svg\u8232 Result: SVG render URLs for unique icons\

\f0\b \'97
\f1\b0  PNG/SVG bytes from those URLs\uc0\u8232 Not a Figma API call. Files land in src/assets/\

\f0\b \'97
\f1\b0  node scripts/inspect-figma.js\uc0\u8232 No API. Prints sections / colors from JSON\

\f0\b \'97
\f1\b0  node scripts/generate-react.js --all\uc0\u8232 No API. Writes src/generated/*.jsx and *.css\
Calls 2 and 3 live in one script so you only run the downloader once.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 What you change per project\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Only these values. The script logic stays the same.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 .env \uc0\u8594  FIGMA_TOKEN
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Figma \u8594  Settings \u8594  Personal access tokens\

\f0\b .env \uc0\u8594  FIGMA_FILE_ID
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 From the URL: figma.com/design/FILE_ID/...\

\f0\b .env \uc0\u8594  FIGMA_NODE_ID
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 URL node-id=2683-6274 becomes 2683:6274 (dash \u8594  colon)\

\f0\b download-figma-images.js \uc0\u8594  ICON_NAME_HINTS
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Extra layer-name words that mean \'93this is an icon\'94\

\f0\b generate-react.js \uc0\u8594  SKIP_SECTION_NAMES
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Decorations you do not want as React pages\

\f0\b generate-react.js \uc0\u8594  FONT_FAMILY
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Font from inspect / Figma text styles\
Do not put the token in the scripts. Keep it in .env (already gitignored in Vite apps).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Steps (stop at generate --all)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Run every command from the project root (the folder that contains package.json).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 1. Create the app in VS Code\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 npm create vite@latest my-figma-app -- --template react\uc0\u8232 cd my-figma-app\u8232 npm install\u8232 npm install axios dotenv
\f1\fs24 \
Optional Tailwind (not required for generate):\

\f2\fs26 npm install tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Create .env at the project root\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Copy .env.example from this kit, or create .env:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 FIGMA_TOKEN=figd_your_token_here\uc0\u8232 FIGMA_FILE_ID=tNmHG9JljZSXLiMs0EWjvG\u8232 FIGMA_NODE_ID=2683:6274
\f1\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Node id rule:
\f1\b0  Figma URL uses a dash; the API uses a colon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 https://www.figma.com/design/FILE_ID/File-Name?node-id=2683-6274\uc0\u8232 \u8594  2683:6274
\f1\fs24 \
Click one frame / one page in Figma (not the whole file). Fetching the entire file wastes quota and makes a huge JSON.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Copy the scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Copy this kit\'92s scripts/ folder into your app:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 my-figma-app/\uc0\u8232 .env\u8232 package.json\u8232 scripts/\u8232 fetch-figma.js\u8232 download-figma-images.js\u8232 generate-react.js\u8232 inspect-figma.js (optional, 0 API calls)
\f1\fs24 \
Confirm package.json has "type": "module" (Vite React template already does).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4. Fetch layout JSON \'97 API call 1 / 3\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 node scripts/fetch-figma.js
\f1\fs24 \
Success: Saved figma-node.json\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Stop.
\f1\b0  Do not run this again for the same design.\
If it fails: token, file id, or node id is wrong. Fix .env and run once.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 5. Inspect locally \'97 0 API calls\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 node scripts/inspect-figma.js
\f1\fs24 \
Prints the page name and top-level section names (these names are what --all will turn into components).\
One section:\

\f2\fs26 node scripts/inspect-figma.js Header\uc0\u8232 node scripts/inspect-figma.js "Hero Section"
\f1\fs24 \
Use this to fill SKIP_SECTION_NAMES and ICON_NAME_HINTS before downloading icons.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 6. Download photos + icons \'97 API calls 2 and 3 / 3\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 node scripts/download-figma-images.js
\f1\fs24 \
Success: Done. Assets in src/assets/images and src/assets/icons\
Writes:\
src/assets/images/ \'97 photos (IMAGE fills)\uc0\u8232 src/assets/icons/ \'97 unique SVG icons\u8232 src/assets/manifest.json \'97 map used by the generator\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Stop.
\f1\b0  Do not run this again unless Figma images changed.\
If icons are missing: add words from those layer names to ICON_NAME_HINTS in download-figma-images.js, then run the downloader once more (that spends 2 more API calls). Prefer getting hints right the first time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 7. Generate React \'97 0 API calls (last required step)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Every top-level section:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 node scripts/generate-react.js --all
\f1\fs24 \
Or one section (name = Figma layer name):\

\f2\fs26 node scripts/generate-react.js Header\uc0\u8232 node scripts/generate-react.js "Hero Section"
\f1\fs24 \
Writes src/generated/Header.jsx, Header.css, and the same for each section.\
You can re-run generate as many times as you want. It only reads figma-node.json and src/assets/manifest.json.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 After --all (not required for the 3-call pipeline)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Wire generated files into src/App.jsx, run npm run dev, then polish CSS by hand. That uses zero Figma API calls.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Do / don\'92t\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Do
\f1\b0 \
\'95 Fetch one node (one frame), not the whole file\uc0\u8232 \'95 Keep .env out of git\u8232 \'95 Re-run generate-react.js freely\

\f0\b Don\'92t
\f1\b0 \
\'95 Call Figma from the browser (src/api/figma.js on every refresh)\uc0\u8232 \'95 Re-run fetch-figma.js or download-figma-images.js \'93to be sure\'94\u8232 \'95 Put FIGMA_TOKEN in a script or in chat\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Troubleshooting\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Missing FIGMA_TOKEN
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 .env at project root, names exactly as in .env.example\

\f0\b Node \'85 not in figma-node.json
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 FIGMA_NODE_ID must match the id used at fetch time (colon, not dash)\

\f0\b figma-node.json not found
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Run fetch-figma.js first, from the project root\

\f0\b Empty / missing icons
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Extend ICON_NAME_HINTS, then download once\

\f0\b Decorative junk as a page
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Add its Figma name to SKIP_SECTION_NAMES\

\f0\b 403 / rate limit
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Stop. Use the JSON already on disk. Wait before any new fetch\
}